al","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tracey Roberts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10994","person_slug":"tracey-roberts","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zoe Daniel","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10979","person_slug":"zoe-daniel","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zoe McKenzie","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10976","person_slug":"zoe-mckenzie","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Business — Rearrangement","noes":12,"question":"Tony Burke I rise to advise members on the order of proceedings as they will now occur. The Counter-Terrorism Legislation Amendment (Prohibited Hate Symbols and Other Measures) Bill 2023 is still being debated in the Federation Chamber. My intention is not to bring that back to here until around 7 pm. In the interim, in a moment I will call on the Australian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Repudiation) Bill 2023, and once that is concluded we will bring back the Economic Inclusion Advisory Committee Bill 2023. In respect of the Australian Citizenship Amendment (Citizenship Repudiation) Bill 2023, I move the contingency motion on the _Notice Paper_: That so much of the standing and sessional orders be suspended as would prevent: (1) debate on the second reading resuming immediately, with the time limit for Members speaking being five minutes; and (2) the second reading debate continuing for no longer than one hour, after which the bill being passed through all its stages without delay. Given that some people are going to be here quite late tonight, I think people know why I'm doing it. There will be different views, but I'll leave it at that. Paul Fletcher In the interest of facilitating this matter, as the opposition has agreed with the government that we will, I won't speak for long, although I do indicate that the opposition will be calling a division on this motion because it is very bad practice to be crunching down debate in this way. That has been our consistent position; we've been maintaining that. I also move: That all words in paragraph (1) after \"immediately\" be omitted with a view to substituting the following words: \"with the time limit for the Member for Wannon being 10 minutes, and the time limit for all other Members speaking being five minutes\". The merits of that motion speak for themselves, given the excellence of the member for Wannon, so I won't speak to it further. Adam Bandt This is outrageous! We are dealing with one of the most fundamenta","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-10310","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2023-11-29/10"}
